    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with **Kyle Tucker** (73.86) acting as the clear anchor of our offense. Facing Canning, **Kyle Tucker** benefits from a high-efficiency matchup against a suspect arm, and his position in the heart of the order provides the stability we need for R/RBI accumulation. **Josh Jung** (68.56) follows closely as our second strongest play, bolstered by a significant 19% SP skill advantage against Peralta. We are also leaning heavily on the top-of-the-order potential of **Sam Antonacci** (61.94); his 0.400 xwOBA and the leadoff slot against Miller\u2019s 4.74 xERA make him a primary engine for our Runs category today. **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (60.88) rounds out the high-priority group, as his ability to consistently reach base outweighs the marginal penalty of a neutral platoon matchup.\n\nOur decision to bench **Nolan Schanuel** (54.92) was the most difficult call of the morning. While he maintains a respectable score, he falls just outside our optimized threshold for starting slots, primarily because his slot in the lower third of the lineup caps his volume potential compared to the high-leverage positions held by **Andy Pages** (60.03) or **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (57.07). We remain cautious regarding **Nasim Nunez** (40.57); while he sits at the floor of our starting requirements, his elite sprint speed makes him a necessary evil in our pursuit of scarce stolen bases, despite the negative drag from his #9 spot in the order. We are keeping a close watch on **Gunnar Henderson** (58.15); while he faces a decent arm in Jax, he provides a subtle boost due to the opponent's slow delivery, which may provide the opening he needs to swipe a base. As always, our injury-riddled bench remains thin, with **Jacob Wilson** and **Jordan Westburg** still sidelined, forcing us to lean heavily on the remaining active core to maximize our efficiency scores without exceeding our season game caps.",
